      "role": "user",
      "content": "thanks for that. it's a good start, but i think it's a little bit \"dry\" for the Gastronomy Weekly style. we usually want something a bit more lush and descriptive so people can really taste it when they read.\n\nthe tool actually just ran your draft and gave it a richness score of 14. for a paragraph this size, that's actually pretty low for our standards—it's barely hitting the 'basic' threshold. \n\ncan you take another pass at it? try to make the descriptions much more vivid and sensory. just please, i'm serious, don't just throw adjectives in for no reason. i want it to be high-quality and evocative, not just a list of words. try to get that score up a bit by actually painting a picture with the language.",
      "source": "evaluator"
